# Mycosynth Lattice's "players may spend mana as though it were mana of any color" is read as the mana is spent (CR 609.4b,
# 611.3a), after the activation's chance to activate mana abilities (CR 602.2b, 601.2g-h). Bot1 activates Goblin Balloon
# Brigade's "{R}: This creature gains flying until end of turn" with the Lattice out and, in the activation's mana window, has
# Krark-Clan Ironworks sacrifice the Lattice for {C}{C}: the Lattice is gone when the cost is paid, so the {C}{C} can't pay
# the {R} and the window stays open - with the Lattice still applying it would have closed by itself, the pool covering the
# cost. The Mountain's {R} pays it, and the {C}{C} is left in the pool.
# Turn 1: the Mountain for the Brigade, two Black Lotuses for the Lattice. Turn 3: a Lotus and an Island for the Ironworks.

